d_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Summary\nMarkdown formulas are shown as raw source (`$...$`, `$$...$$`, `\\(...\\)`, `\\[...\\]`) instead of rendered math in Trae preview.\n\n## Environment\n- Product: Trae IDE\n- OS: macOS\n- Workspace: local project markdown files\n- Repro file: `latex_formula_test.md`\n\n## What I already tried\n- Enabled math settings in user/workspace `settings.json`:\n  - `markdown.math.enabled: true`\n  - `markdown.extension.katex.macros: {}`\n  - switched/removed conflicting markdown math settings\n- Reloaded window\n- Tested multiple delimiter styles and math blocks\n- Added comprehensive test markdown with inline/block/aligned/matrix/fenced math\n\n## Reproduction Steps\n1. Open any `.md` file in Trae.\n2. Add formulas like:\n   - `$e^{i\\pi}+1=0$`\n   - `$$\\int_0^1 x^2\\,dx=\\frac{1}{3}$$`\n   - `\\(a^2+b^2=c^2\\)`\n   - `\\[\\sum_{k=1}^{n}k=\\frac{n(n+1)}{2}\\]`\n3. Open markdown preview.\n\n## Actual Behavior\nFormulas are not rendered and appear as plain LaTeX source text.\n\n## Expected Behavior\nAll supported LaTeX/KaTeX formulas should render normally in markdown preview.\n\n## Additional Notes\n- This started/was noticed after updating Trae.\n- Similar conflict patterns exist in VS Code ecosystem when multiple math providers collide, but issue persists even after reducing settings and trying isolated syntax variants.\n- Please advise if there is a current known regression or recommended stable preview pipeline in Trae.\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Trae-AI/TRAE/issues/2480/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Trae-AI/TRAE/issues/2480/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null},"comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Trae-AI/TRAE/issues/comments/4530904485","html_url":"https://github.com/Trae-AI/TRAE/issues/2480#